# File Organization

One file, one job. A reader should guess a file's purpose from its path and name.

## Layout

Group by feature, not by type:

```
src/
  app/              # pages / entry points
  features/
    auth/           # login, session — all in one folder
    posts/          # list, detail, create
  shared/           # reused UI, hooks, utils (only if used twice+)
  styles/
```

## Naming

- Files: `kebab-case` (`user-card.jsx`, `fetch-posts.js`)
- Components: match the export (`UserCard` lives in `user-card.jsx`)
- Folders: short and specific (`auth`, `posts`) — not `misc`, `helpers`, `stuff`

## Size and splits

- Keep files under ~150 lines. Split when a file covers two topics
- Colocate: a component, its styles, and its tiny helpers stay in the same folder
- Put a file in `shared/` only after a second feature needs it
- Don't create empty folders or "utils.js" dumping grounds

## Don't

- Don't mix unrelated features in one file
- Don't nest folders more than 3 levels under `src/`
- Don't duplicate the same helper in three places — extract to `shared/` then
